    "body": "Displays the git information for the current Hazel build as an unobtrusive, always-visible indicator in the top-right of the top bar, plus in the page title, so it's clear which build you're looking at when juggling multiple branches/tabs. Originally written by @7h3kk1d and developed by @CyrusD123; design revised per review discussion (the earlier git-icon slide-out panel was heavier than this information warrants).\n\n## What it shows\n\n`branch@short-sha[-ahead][-dirty] \u00b7 #PR`, in a color only slightly darker than the top-bar background \u2014 legible if you look for it, invisible if you don't.\n\n- **branch** links to the branch on GitHub; **short-sha** links to the commit (links always present; an unpushed commit's link starts working after push).\n- **`-ahead`** marks commits not yet pushed to the upstream branch; **`-dirty`** marks uncommitted local changes (addressing the request to distinguish these).\n- **`\u00b7 #NNNN`** appears when the branch has an open PR, linked to it. Detected at build time via the `gh` CLI (`scripts/build-info.sh`) \u2014 an *optional* dependency: if `gh` is missing, unauthenticated, offline, or there's no open PR, the segment is simply omitted. Since the `BuildInfo.ml` rule re-runs on every rebuild and the `gh` call costs ~0.4s, the lookup is cached per branch in `.git/hazel-pr-cache` (steady-state rebuilds pay ~0.06s, same as the git-only rule); a `pre-push` hook deletes the cache since the answer most often changes around pushes. The hook activates once the `core.hooksPath` installation from #2233 lands; until then (or without `gh`), staleness is bounded by branch switches, and deleting the cache file forces a re-query.\n- The **page title** becomes `hazel \u00b7 branch@sha[-suffix]`, except on a clean, pushed `dev` build where it stays plain `hazel`.\n\n## Selectability\n\nThe label is drag-selectable for copying to a collaborator \u2014 you can start the selection anywhere in the top bar's empty space and sweep across. This took some spelunking: mousedown over non-focusable page regions moves focus to `#page`, whose `on_blur` handler re-focuses the clipboard shim mid-gesture, destroying the nascent selection (the sidebar avoids this only because it has a `tabindex`). Fixes: `tabindex=\"-1\"` on the indicator so it swallows focus like the sidebar; exemptions in the `#page` copy/cut handlers so Cmd+C copies the selected label rather than the editor selection (and Cmd+X doesn't delete editor content); sidebar-style `user-select` descendant rules; non-draggable anchors; and the label kept as a single inline span (selection across flex items is unreliable). The same tabindex + exemption treatment could make other UI text selectable in future PRs.\n\n## Removed\n\nThe bottom-bar git-icon slide-out panel, its `build_info_expanded` setting, the git icon asset, and the associated CSS.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Indicator renders with branch/sha links; `-ahead`/`-dirty` suffixes appear and disappear as commits are made/pushed (observed live during development)\n- [x] Open-PR detection: `BuildInfo.ml` generated with `Some 2315` + URL on this branch; `None` fallback verified with `gh` off PATH\n- [x] PR cache lifecycle: first build writes `.git/hazel-pr-cache`; cache hit serves the PR with no network (verified with `gh` off PATH); `pre-push` hook invalidates; post-invalidation build without `gh` degrades to `None`\n- [x] Drag-selection from empty bar space, glyphs (both directions), padding, and bar edge \u2014 verified via automated CDP tests in headless Chrome\n- [x] Copy event over a build-info selection passes through natively (clipboard shim untouched); editor copy/cut behavior unchanged elsewhere\n- [x] Page title: `hazel \u00b7 branch@sha-suffix` on this branch; plain `hazel` on clean dev\n- [ ] Reviewer: sanity-check on a machine without `gh` installed\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01RXiW9jhHvYfwpwBT15MCwW\n",
